#{[17592186369502 #edb/ref 1080 "16\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369502 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369502 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "808c516e-8fb0-5d9d-b3c3-71bd5e0c0d18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369503 #edb/ref 1080 "18\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369503 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369503 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56bd1130-5922-503b-9779-186620077dd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369525 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369525 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126945" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369525 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369525 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/75/754aa1ded10b20362350f3da9e5b4dbe5f9f194c2289af348ff9de34f2fb8cc5.png)\n\nCalculate \n${∮}_{∂D}(x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3})\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3})\\,dy,$\nwhere $D$ is the region shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369525 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "904872cd-e02c-55d9-9792-17de482b0907" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369525 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}$ and $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4xy.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}(x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3})\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4xy-2xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be represented in Cartesian coordinates as ${Δ}_{1}∖{Δ}_{2},$ where\n\n- ${Δ}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,-1\\le y\\le 2\\}$ is the region enclosed by the outer curve, and\n\n- ${Δ}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,0\\le y\\le 1\\}$ is the region enclosed by the inner curve.\n\nTherefore, our double integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{{Δ}_{1}}2xy\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{{Δ}_{2}}2xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}2xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{-1}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{1}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(4-4)\\cdot (2-\\frac{1}{2})-(1-1)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}-0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369526 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369526 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369526 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186369531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369526 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1303c02b-a3ee-52e9-98a2-763dbec18e4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369527 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369527 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369527 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "006e746d-7483-59b3-ba9c-8cd280691f9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186