10b7-5658-8197-b5afed861eb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498381 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498381 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498381 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498381 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498381 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498381 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498381 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498381 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186498270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498381 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "30362ef7-7428-53da-a7f2-7fe7cc3d3d5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186497887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498438 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a7d01b58-0857-54fb-bdf6-61d33e711eeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498490 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498490 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126895" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498490 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498490 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0d/0db447407835f74476edd20ed5327ff3cc570905f744bbc6c29a66926913ecb5.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}(1-4y)\\,dx+(2+5x)\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498490 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "09c35a82-4469-5857-aed4-331c374b8ab3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498490 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=1-4y$ and $Q(x,y)=2+5x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}dx+x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-(-4))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot 5\\pi  \\\\  & =45\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126851" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e9/e9892ef4efa3481ad02f7b8e38f1bae1876b196627204521d011656010297281.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=16,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=6,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=4,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2260d96-b984-5295-801c-28a9593008a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498590 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/b2/b20b2b911c2a417c26fa951d9b28efa296c265df25e9d06b635ef4846267b93b.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =16+6+4 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498611 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498611 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b31cf93-d5e4-581a-abf0-1f4ce4b0318a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498611 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186369434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498614 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498614 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2056fd1b-d5a8-5347-8cd3-9a0ecc4618d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498614 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186369462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498629 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498629 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6fb02394-525d-5f30-9775-578f4448db13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498629 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498640 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "96ebff15-a11c-5705-a99b-83a08193b653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498640 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498650 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498650 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c3cbee15-50e1-5853-bd12-2ab6e6059abb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498650 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1045 "Extending Green's Theorem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186519648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518984 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "b43c564a-026d-55f8-9ded-681ee43fa117" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518998 #edb/ref 1080 "70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518998 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518998 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0662a46f-bec7-54ca-b240-f60d5d5f1afc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519013 #edb/ref 1080 "50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519013 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519013 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e19b2e0-2b38-57c0-b50d-3e99a4fb345c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519022 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519022 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519022 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "12efe453-d9bc-5e34-bdeb-04e1a1d22aee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519256 #edb/ref 1080 "20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519256 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519256 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a0fe6c9c-6868-551d-8a19-e70fb67ab8d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519334 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519334 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519334 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d13ea829-20bc-5000-ad9a-b878fad5ad6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186519013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186519022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186519256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186519334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519450 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519450 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519450 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186518998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519450 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "69041780-f401-5aab-a5e0-f58cc39dca02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519559 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186519450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519559 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126866" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519559 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519559 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0f/0f1dd3c66e3bf7d25f286720b360d6af1d6361804ab3ff52835d94f78e5084ee.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}-3y\\,dx+2x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519559 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "881df761-fca2-5afa-aea8-d6a6e63a7521" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519559 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-3y$ and $Q(x,y)=2x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-3,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-3y\\,dx+2x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2-(-3))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =5\\cdot ({4}^{2}-\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{2}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (16-2) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519610 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186519667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519610 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "02b0f97c-a1c4-5de3-9e6c-ca0b67ea4390" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519610 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186369469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519631 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186519610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519631 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "48cb7736-a399-57ef-8551-b03d268a4144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519631 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186369455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519647 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7855bb63-c81b-53d8-a3eb-d50bbb715b43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519647 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186441618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519648 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186519631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519648 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8b29823e-1d02-5228-87de-cfdd6eddac82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519648 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186431351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519667 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186519647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519667 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dcca2676-1c39-51b2-9647-11d87db779a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519667 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186519559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538151 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538179 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186538151 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186538151 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/57/573013be1dc56a1ae4d0765b81b8e94006b8402a6da9706b118d43e286fb8291.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}6y\\,dx+9x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186538151 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0093dc0f-6d13-5136-8a41-4ec719538cf8" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186538151 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=6y$ and $Q(x,y)=9x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=6,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}6y\\,dx+9x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(9-6)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{17\\pi}{2}  \\\\  & =\\frac{51\\pi}{2} .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186538156 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538154 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186538156 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186538156 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1e/1e97d150acbe82bf31d0a0e371122ae567d62279b66a5db2a3164180248a5e71.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}-13dx+12x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186538156 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28489039-fdfa-503c-aed0-769a751abddb" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186538156 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-13$ and $Q(x,y)=12x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-13dx+12x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(12-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {5}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {4}^{2}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (25\\pi -16\\pi ) \\\\  & =108\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
